#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/tt-bundling.md:6
msgid "TT Bundling"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/tt-bundling.md:8
msgid ""
"When designing recursive or multi-layered declarative macros, passing around "
"a large number of parameters individually can make patterns messy and "
"difficult to maintain."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/tt-bundling.md:12
msgid ""
"**TT Bundling** is a pattern where multiple arguments are grouped together "
"inside a single token group (e.g., `(param1: arg1, parmam2: arg2)`), "
"allowing them to be passed them through layers of recursion as a single "
"unified `tt` metavariable:"
msgstr ""

